From: =?UTF-8?q?Robin=20Br=C3=A4mer?= <robin.braemer@web.de>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] loader: skip unresolved identifiers when listing options

`OptionHelpExtractor::walk_call_expr` unwrapped the symbol of every
called identifier. A call whose identifier has no resolved symbol, such
as `str(x)` inside a config literal of a schema from a package the
loader did not resolve, panicked; on wasm32 (panic=abort) that traps the
whole instance, so `list_options` failed for an ordinary Package such as
`corev1.ConfigMap { data.replicas = str(input.replicas) }`. Such an
identifier cannot be the builtin `option`: skip it.
---
diff --git a/crates/loader/src/option.rs b/crates/loader/src/option.rs
--- a/crates/loader/src/option.rs
+++ b/crates/loader/src/option.rs
@@ -22,8 +22,15 @@
                 pkgpath: self.pkgpath.clone(),
                 id: identifier.names[0].id.clone(),
             };
-            let symbol_ref = self.packages.node_symbol_map.get(&node_key).unwrap();
-            let symbol = self.packages.symbols.get(symbol_ref).unwrap();
+            // An identifier without a resolved symbol (inside a config whose
+            // schema type did not resolve, say) cannot be the builtin
+            // `option`: skip it instead of panicking, which aborts on wasm32.
+            let Some(symbol_ref) = self.packages.node_symbol_map.get(&node_key) else {
+                return;
+            };
+            let Some(symbol) = self.packages.symbols.get(symbol_ref) else {
+                return;
+            };
             let binding = &BUILTIN_FUNCTIONS;
             let builtin_option_type = binding.get("option").unwrap();
             if !symbol.is_global
